                        "glosses": [
                            "The water monitor, Varanus salvator, a large lizard of Southeast Asia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d005ce9-bc88-432b-b2e4-a3f65d82ca5f",
                                "sense_id": "ef430fe6-68f3-36eb-901e-78ad5a0346c9",
                                "text": "The Chairman said that Kegalla raised the question of protecting the Kabaragoya from destruction and the Department of Agriculture took up the matter[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5704ee9e-c5be-4264-b6ac-6e9abe460ac7",
                                "sense_id": "ef430fe6-68f3-36eb-901e-78ad5a0346c9",
                                "text": "[…]I remember after-school cricket matches on Layard's Road and wickets knocked over by kabaragoyas;[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7a8e8fe-0a44-4c2c-a590-a2c8461165ba",
                                "sense_id": "ef430fe6-68f3-36eb-901e-78ad5a0346c9",
                                "text": "Cobras had nothing to fear from men; their most deadly enemy was the kabaragoya, of which two called our campus home."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6b37346-3092-42a6-8f7e-d1034c4d0b89",
                                "sense_id": "ef430fe6-68f3-36eb-901e-78ad5a0346c9",
                                "text": "2012, Arcadius (Shelton A. Gunaratne), Village Life in the Forties: Memories of a Lankan Expatriate, page 150,\nA kabaragoya, scenting food, tried to drive away the crows, slashing at them with its tail."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
